From: Karol Hirsz <karol.hirsz@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mtd: spi-nor: add support for GigaDevice MD25D40

Legacy 512 KiB GigaDevice NOR flash found in Keemple KP-GW-01.
It reports the old 0x51 manufacturer ID and has no SFDP tables,
so it is not picked up by the generic SFDP fallback either.

4K sector erase is not enabled until confirmed on hardware,
64 KiB block erase is used instead.

Signed-off-by: Karol Hirsz <karol.hirsz@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/mtd/spi-nor/gigadevice.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/mtd/spi-nor/gigadevice.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/spi-nor/gigadevice.c
@@ -95,6 +95,11 @@ static const struct flash_info gigadevic
 		.size = SZ_16M,
 		.flags = SPI_NOR_HAS_LOCK | SPI_NOR_HAS_TB,
 		.no_sfdp_flags = SECT_4K | SPI_NOR_DUAL_READ | SPI_NOR_QUAD_READ,
+	}, {
+		/* legacy part with 0x51 manufacturer ID, no SFDP */
+		.id = SNOR_ID(0x51, 0x40, 0x13),
+		.name = "md25d40",
+		.size = SZ_512K,
 	},
 };

